{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: Merge `addPRLabelQuietly` and `addPRLabelQuietlyDetailed`**

The two helpers are the same operation differing only in whether success is logged:

```javascript
function addPRLabelQuietly(scm, prNumber, label, okMessage, warnPrefix) {
    try {
        scm.addLabel(prNumber, label);
        console.log(okMessage);
    } catch (labelErr) {
        console.warn(warnPrefix, labelErr);
    }
}

function addPRLabelQuietlyDetailed(scm, prNumber, label, warnPrefix) {
    try {
        scm.addLabel(prNumber, label);
    } catch (prLabelError) {
        console.warn(warnPrefix, prLabelError.message || prLabelError);
    }
}
```

Make the success message optional (`if (okMessage) console.log(okMessage)`) and keep a single helper — this file's whole theme is named, single-purpose steps, and two near-identical "quietly" variants reintroduces the copy-paste pattern the PR set out to remove. Also note the warn argument shapes differ (`labelErr` vs `labelErr.message || labelErr`) — one more reason to unify.
